return {
["08:00"]={"His landlady’s cook, who always brought him his breakfast at \003eight o’clock\004, failed to appear on this occasion. That had never happened before.","The Trial","Franz Kafka"},
["08:01"]={"\003Eight-one\004, tick-tock, eight-one o’clock, off to school, off to work, run, run, eight-one!","There Will Come Soft Rains","Ray Bradbury"},
["08:02"]={"\003Eight oh two\004 eh em, Death of Corporal Littlebottombottom … Eight oh three eh em … Death of Sergeant Detritus … Eight oh threethreethree eh em and seven seconds seconds … Death of Constable Visit … Eight oh three eh em and nineninenine seconds … Death of death of death of …","Jingo","Terry Pratchett"},
["08:03"]={"When he had finished the last mouthful, Scott checked his watch: \003three minutes past eight\004—just enough time for coffee before grabbing a taxi to the airport.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:04"]={"\0038:04 A.M.\004\nThe phone was ringing, but Mark was still in a deep sleep. It continued to ring.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:05"]={"Well, it’s \003five-past eight\004 now, I said to Drake. “You’d better go straight off and organise a flashing party. There’s not a hope of a sortie tonight at sea, but we’d better be on the safe side.”","Eight Hours from England","Anthony Quayle"},
["08:06"]={"I had a restless night with some fever and was a little late starting out. It was \003six minutes past eight\004 when I arrived at the lighthouse. I was unable to gain entry. The door was locked.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James"},
["08:07"]={"It was \003seven minutes past eight\004 when Lara saw Betty Jeffries hurrying towards the school with her children in tow.","Dreams Beneath a Red Sun","Elizabeth Haran"},
["08:09"]={"He looked across at his son. ‘You been booking in all those names, the way I taught you?’\n‘Sure have, Dad. Mr Parnell, 7:47; Mr Parker, \0038:09\004; Mr Tudor-Jones, 8:11; Mr Alexander, 8:23.’","The Grass is Always Greener","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:10"]={"Sloane, with his shoulder punctured, was on another lounge. He was half delirious, and kept calling something about a chemistry lecture at \0038:10.\004","This Side of Paradise","F. Scott Fitzgerald"},
["08:11"]={"He looked across at his son. ‘You been booking in all those names, the way I taught you?’\n‘Sure have, Dad. Mr Parnell, 7:47; Mr Parker, 8:09; Mr Tudor-Jones, \0038:11\004; Mr Alexander, 8:23.’","The Grass is Always Greener","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:13"]={"At \0038:13 a.m.\004 the alarm clock in the laboratory gave the ringing word. Eddie touched a button in the substructure of an ordinary glass coffeepot, from whose spout two tubes proceeded into the wall.","In Time Which Made a Monkey of Us All","Grace Paley"},
["08:14"]={"At \003fourteen minutes past eight\004, a man came in, wearing a sheepskin coat. He was sucking on a hand-rolled cigarette. The man stuck out his hand, cheerfully. “You’ll be Mister Moon,” he said.","The Monarch of the Glen","Neil Gaiman"},
["08:15"]={"“Get me the head of the Secret Service at the White House.”\n“Yes, sir.”\nThe Director glanced at his watch: 7:10. Andrews was due at \0038:15\004. The phone rang.","Shall We Tell the President?","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:17"]={"“Then let’s get going,” said T. Hamilton McKenzie. He checked his watch. It was \0038:17\004. With a bit of luck he might still make the meeting on time.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:18"]={"Say they left at seventeen or \003eighteen minutes past eight\004. In that case they must have followed Joanne Garland and might well be driving faster than she.","Kissing the Gunner’s Daughter","Ruth Rendell"},
["08:19"]={"At \0038:19\004 she received a second phone call to let her know the plane had taken off from Amman with the “cargo” on board.","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:20"]={"This morning I took the launch out for forty minutes or so to test the engine. She’s been giving a bit of trouble. That took from seven-forty-five until \003twenty past eight\004, near enough.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James"},
["08:21"]={"Midnight barked from the backyard, then someone knocked on my front door. Hard. I looked at the time on my phone, \0038:21 a.m.\004 Once late for me to start my day, but always early for someone to knock on the door uninvited.","Lost Tomorrows","Matt Coyle"},
["08:22"]={"Daisy Flory made her 999 call at \003twenty-two minutes past eight\004, within a few minutes of their leaving.","Kissing the Gunner’s Daughter","Ruth Rendell"},
["08:23"]={"At \0038:23\004 there seemed every chance of a lasting alliance starting between Florin and Guilder. At 8:24 the two nations were very close to war.","The Princess Bride","William Goldman"},
["08:24"]={"At 8:23 there seemed every chance of a lasting alliance starting between Florin and Guilder. At \0038:24\004 the two nations were very close to war.","The Princess Bride","William Goldman"},
["08:25"]={"The next day, Jay sat at his desk promptly at eight. At \003twenty-five after\004, Irene came over. “Time to go to the meeting.”\nJay stood. “Who’ll take over the phones?”","The Arachne Portal","Joan Marie Verba"},
["08:26"]={"He turned around and asked the youth, “What’s the time?” The young man looked proudly at his new acquisition, which he hadn’t taken his eyes off for one moment.\n“\003Twenty-six minutes after eight\004 and twenty seconds.”","Honor Among Thieves","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:27"]={"On arriving at platform one at Sevenoaks station, he would purchase a copy of the Daily Express before boarding the \0038:27\004 to Cannon Street.","Broken Routine","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:28"]={"And at \0038:28\004 on the following morning, with a novel chilliness about the upper lip, and a vast excess of strength and spirits, I was sitting in a third-class carriage, bound for Germany, and dressed as a young sea-man, in a pea-jacket, peaked cap, and comforter.","The Riddle of the Sands","Erskine Childers"},
["08:29"]={"Mr. Trent himself followed a rigid routine. Each day, he arose at 7 a.m., breakfasted at 7:30, and departed for work at 8:10, arriving at \0038:29\004.","The Great Train Robbery","Michael Crichton"},
["08:30"]={"When he woke, at \003eight-thirty\004, he was alone in the bedroom. He put on his dressing gown and put in his hearing aid and went into the living room.","Deaf Sentence","David Lodge"},
["08:31"]={"At \0038:31 a.m.\004, MST, a woman on TWA’s Flight 196 burst into tears and began to bugle her own opinion, which was perhaps not unshared among some other passengers (or even the crew, for that matter), that the plane was going to crash.","The Shining","Stephen King"},
["08:32"]={"He woke again with a start when the hardback of The Last Chronicle of Barset thudded to the ground. Fumbling for his watch, he saw with dismay that it was \003eight thirty-two\004, a late start to the day.","The Lighthouse","P.D. James"},
["08:33"]={"It’s too late for any TV because of the cake, watch says it is \00308:33\004. My yellow hoody nearly rips my head off when Ma is pulling it.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["08:34"]={"At \00308:34 hours\004 precisely General Conrad Pyne’s black official Rover 800 stopped outside the ugly wrought iron barrier that guarded the entrance into Downing Street.","Doomsday Ultimatum","James Follett"},
["08:35"]={"OLD GUMMY GRANNY: (THRUSTS A DAGGER TOWARDS STEPHEN’S HAND) Remove him, acushla. At \0038:35 a.m.\004 you will be in heaven and Ireland will be free. (SHE PRAYS) O good God, take him!","Ulysses","James Joyce"},
["08:36"]={"The first maroon had been fired at \00308:36\004 and the second a few moments later. The puffs of green smoke from the maroons were still hanging in the sky above when Pete arrived, breathless but still running.","Lifeboat!","Margaret Dickinson"},
["08:37"]={"\003Eight thirty-seven\004 a.m., Patrice Lane, Biohazard: The dog’s clean. The Good Samaritan was a woman with an accent of some sort. Why haven’t you called me?","Magic Bleeds","Ilona Andrews"},
["08:38"]={"Vasquez’s car was stopped at Carfraemill — at \00308:38 hours\004, he pointed out.\n“Aye —annd—?”\n“Heading north, mon!” he snapped.","A Deviant Breed","Stephen Coill"},
["08:39"]={"Doug McGuire noticed the early hour, \0038:39 A.M.\004 on the one wall clock that gave Daylight Savings Time for the East Coast.","Terminal Compromise","Winn Schwartau"},
["08:40"]={"He left the Sherry-Netherland just after \0038:40\004, and by the time he reached Lexington, he was just about ready to face the headmaster’s wrath.","Cometh the Hour","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:41"]={"It’s \00308:41\004 and I’m in Bed practicing. Ma’s filled a plastic bag with really hot water and tied it tight so none spills out, she puts it in another bag and ties that too.","Room","Emma Donoghue"},
["08:42"]={"When Black himself finally appeared at \003eighteen minutes to nine\004, she became very engrossed in the details of Wednesday’s surveillance. So engrossed, in fact, the she barely noticed him standing in the door of her space until he spoke.","His Hot Number","Shannon Hollis"},
["08:43"]={"You understand this tape recorder is on?\n“Uh huh”\n“And it’s Wednesday, May 15, at \003eight forty-three\004 in the mornin’.”\n“If you say so”","A Time to Kill","John Grisham"},
["08:44"]={"Several soldiers — some with their uniforms unbuttoned — were looking over a motorcycle, arguing about it. The sergeant looked at his watch; it was \003eight forty-four\004. They had to wait until nine. Hladik, feeling more insignificant than ill-fortuned, sat down on a pile of firewood.","The Secret Miracle","Jorge Luis Borges"},
["08:45"]={"DAVID ARRIVED AT the office at 9 A.M. on Monday to find that the front door was locked. He could not understand it. The secretaries were supposed to be in by \0038:45\004.","Not a Penny More, Not a Penny Less","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:47"]={"\0038:47 a.m.\004 Just had fag. But no-smoking day does not start officially till have got dressed.","Bridget Jones’s Diary","Helen Fielding"},
["08:48"]={"Surely if she walked down Swane Street and down Leeds Road, she could go into the old door, up the old steps and slip into her old chair, gather up her old stock of paper and scent and gum, and just go on with her work where she had left off? But it was \003twelve minutes to nine\004.","Courage","Malachi Whitaker"},
["08:49"]={"At \0038:49\004 there was a loud rap on the door, and Sir Hamish muttered an inaudible reproach as David Heath went to open it. He found his contact standing there.","A Matter of Principle","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:50"]={"Punctually at \003ten minutes to nine\004, a quarter hour after early mass, the boy stood in his Sunday uniform outside his father’s door.","The Radetzky March","Joseph Roth"},
["08:51"]={"\0038:51 a.m.\004 Arrive at school","The Curious Incident of the Dog in the Night-Time","Mark Haddon"},
["08:52"]={"Message one. Tuesday, \0038:52 am\004. Is anybody there? Hello?","Extremely Loud and Incredibly Close","Jonathan Safran Foer"},
["08:53"]={"Ross looked out of the window to see Diego Martinez running flat out along the track toward the station. He checked his watch: \0038:53 a.m.\004","Be Careful What You Wish For","Jeffrey Archer"},
["08:54"]={"He had to fork out almost a pound on a taxi to make sure he arrived at the police station at \0038:54 a.m.\004 A young constable took him straight through to Detective Sergeant Warwick’s office, and not an interview room.","Heads You Win","Jeffrey Archer"},
